# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-1 and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch that holds them. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the classes, the minutes, the read rules and the NO-GO rules. Push ONE tag at a time and wait for its run to finish (the workflow keeps one pending run; queued tags are cancelled). Never cancel a running card job.
# AD-A2-production-timed: arm A2 of the ABAB of the adaptive Lever N governor (docs/lever-n-adaptive-governor.md; A = the production profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic, B = its gate-only twin c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-adaptive, which is A plus exactly
# QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_ADAPTIVE=1 and its three defaults written out). ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefill-1 is the PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds (sed -i 's/tp4-prefill-1/<tag>/' *.env); both arms run on it, A with the policy
# unnamed (the image paces as tp4-next2-1 does) and B with it on. Order A1 B1 A2 B2 (ABAB), one tag at a time. Tests: warmup, concurrent8_skew (two cold 254k prompts and six 4k, EIGHT live: the policy is out of force and
# the pacing must be A's, step for step; the slowest first token must stay inside the 238 s limit), concurrent8_code_32k (eight 32k users: the same), and prefill_few_decoders (ONE decoder and a 120k cold prompt, then TWO decoders and
# a 254k one: the policy's own shape, three concurrent requests). TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this block (about 140 minutes), no build, no CI push, no other job beside it.
# READ, in order, stopping at the first failure: (1) the launched argv: profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic, and on B the four QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_ADAPTIVE* names, on A none; (2) c2_smoke_check clean (its levern_adaptive_problems rule: A shows NO adaptive line
# or field, B shows the install line 'lever N adaptive: decoders<=2 share=0.9 ttft=120 gap_floor=8' and base=/target=/adaptive= on every step line, adaptive=1 exactly for the prefill steps with 1 or 2 decoders, and
# prefill_few_decoders EXERCISED); (3) the alternation and decode-gap-floor rules clean in both arms (they run on every step line); (4) `python3 scripts/ci/prefill_ladder_report.py A.json --second B.json`: the few-decoder
# TTFT ratio B over A (ESTIMATED 0.60 to 0.65 for the 254k arrival, 0.55 to 0.65 for the 120k one), the decoders' longest gaps, and the arrival text column 'same' for both shapes (greedy text byte-identical);
# (5) `scripts/ci/w2ln_timing_compare.py` on the eight-live windows (skew, 32k): B inside the A-to-A drift (A1 against A2). NO-GO: any text difference, a floor or alternation problem, a skew slowest first token over the limit,
# an eight-live window outside the drift (the policy must be inert there), a missing adaptive line on B or any on A. Duration (estimate): boot 10 minutes, skew 7, 32k 6, few-decoder shapes 14 (the 254k one rides to its 180 s target on A,
# about 115 to 120 s on B), 40 minutes; the box is 60.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefill-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_skew,concurrent8_code_32k,prefill_few_decoders
# Knowingly omits concurrent8_steady: without this key c2_serving_job.py refuses the job. The smoke check is unchanged, so the run still ends red on its eight-seat rule; read the logs.
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=adaptive governor ABAB: its test list is fixed by the protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
